      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You described feeling immobilized isn't a sign of permanence but of a deep depression that twists your perspective until it seems permanent. Asking if there is no way back is so hauntingly painful, yet it shows you are still searching, which is a small but vital spark left within even the darkest void. Please keep reaching out for support, because healing often begins exactly when we stop believing the emptiness and remember that we still have a future to give meaning to.",
      "source": "target",
